{"status":"complete","spec_files":["tests/guestbook.spec.mjs"],"summary":"Added tests/guestbook.spec.mjs: a flat spec of 6 tests matching smoke.spec.mjs style, one per criterion (add entry with POST payload proof; newest first; counter 0/1 entry/2 entries; stored on server via reload and GET /api/entries; empty message gives "Message is required" with nothing stored, verified after reload and via the API; error cleared after a later successful submit). beforeEach calls POST /api/reset and waits for the page's initial GET /api/entries, because that response would otherwise overwrite a fast submit. Locators use label, role and text, with no test ids.

Verification: baseline smoke spec was green. The new spec passed solo (6/6), with --repeat-each=5 (30/30), and in the full suite (7/7). V2 was checked with temporary inverted-assertion copies (removed afterward) for the order, counter, error-cleared, error-shown and server-stored checks. Each went red at the mutated assertion. V4 is covered by the POST payload and 400 status checks plus the server re-read; I did not inject a failed write for the success path. V3 was not run as a separate route-fault probe. V5 is safe because the state is disposable and reset before every test. V6 was done by a fresh read-only subagent reviewer, whose verdict was "VERDICT: Real P0 = 0".

Not verified or skipped: (a) no live browser exploration ran. The locators come from reading app.mjs and were confirmed only by the passing test runs. (b) The e2e-reviewer scanner script is not an approved command and was not run, so Phase 1 was skipped and the review was manual. The reviewer subagent also did not read the skill's reference files. (c) No control files were written, since the user opted out. The write set is only tests/guestbook.spec.mjs, plus Playwright runtime output (test-results)."}

